WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.130
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.735
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.035 --> 00:00:13.858
Unit twenty-two: Quantifiers. Today you will talk about quantities accurately.

4
00:00:14.158 --> 00:00:16.776
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:21.291
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:23.012
A few.

7
00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:26.980
A few means a small number; countable, positive.

8
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:29.072
I have a few friends.

9
00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:32.545
Your turn. Say: A few.

10
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.378
A few.

11
00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:37.920
A little.

12
00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:42.031
A little means a small amount; uncountable, positive.

13
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:43.920
I have a little time.

14
00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:46.647
Your turn. Say: A little.

15
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.269
A little.

16
00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.018
Plenty of.

17
00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:54.807
Plenty of means more than enough.

18
00:00:55.417 --> 00:00:56.882
There is plenty of food.

19
00:00:57.483 --> 00:00:59.950
Your turn. Say: Plenty of.

20
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.615
Plenty of.

21
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.363
A lot of.

22
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:08.640
A lot of means a large number or amount.

23
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.727
A lot of people came.

24
00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:13.621
Your turn. Say: A lot of.

25
00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:17.479
A lot of.

26
00:01:18.217 --> 00:01:19.113
Several.

27
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:22.708
Several means more than two but not many.

28
00:01:23.317 --> 00:01:25.014
Several students left.

29
00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:27.874
Your turn. Say: Several.

30
00:01:30.733 --> 00:01:31.792
Several.

31
00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.609
Hardly any.

32
00:01:34.617 --> 00:01:36.790
Hardly any means almost none.

33
00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:39.139
Hardly any water is left.

34
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.449
Your turn. Say: Hardly any.

35
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.406
Hardly any.

36
00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:48.105
Countable.

37
00:01:49.117 --> 00:01:51.720
Countable means can be counted: apples.

38
00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:53.724
Apples are countable.

39
00:01:54.317 --> 00:01:56.586
Your turn. Say: Countable.

40
00:01:59.433 --> 00:02:00.458
Countable.

41
00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:02.369
Uncountable.

42
00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:05.929
Uncountable means cannot be counted: water.

43
00:02:06.517 --> 00:02:07.982
Water is uncountable.

44
00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:11.224
Your turn. Say: Uncountable.

45
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.404
Uncountable.

46
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.607
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.390
Visal, describe your weekend using quantifiers.

48
00:02:24.483 --> 00:02:34.963
I had a lot of homework, but there was plenty of time. I saw a few friends and I drank a little coffee. Quantifiers tell us how many or how much.

49
00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.283
How do we choose?

50
00:02:38.383 --> 00:02:52.430
With countable nouns: a few, several, many. With uncountable nouns: a little, much. A lot of and plenty of work with both. Hardly any means almost none, and is used with both.

51
00:02:53.517 --> 00:02:55.841
What is the difference between few and a few?

52
00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:09.961
A few is positive: I have a few friends, so I am not lonely. Few is negative: I have few friends, so I feel alone. The same is true for little and a little.

53
00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.960
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:13.817 --> 00:03:17.860
Grammar focus: Quantifiers with countable and uncountable nouns.

55
00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.254
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.845
I have a few close friends.

57
00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.274
There is a little milk left.

58
00:03:25.183 --> 00:03:27.311
There is plenty of food for everyone.

59
00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:35.998
A few / several + countable. A little + uncountable. A lot of and plenty of + both. Hardly any = almost none.

60
00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:40.366
Be careful! Don't say: I have a few time.

61
00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.358
Say: I have a little time.

62
00:03:44.658 --> 00:03:46.193
Time is uncountable.

63
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.908
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.305
How Many, How Much?.

65
00:03:52.605 --> 00:03:55.069
On Saturday I had a lot of homework.

66
00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:58.182
I met a few friends in the afternoon.

67
00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:02.014
There was plenty of food, and I drank a little juice.

68
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.116
Hardly any people were at the park.

69
00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.959
Several students were there, but only a few stayed.

70
00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:14.022
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:14.883 --> 00:04:18.000
I have blank time. (small amount, uncountable)

72
00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.733
A, a few. B, a little. C, several.

73
00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:26.930
The answer is B: a little.

74
00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:30.817
She has blank friends in the city. (countable)

75
00:04:31.117 --> 00:04:34.248
A, a few. B, a little. C, much.

76
00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.741
The answer is A: a few.

77
00:04:40.883 --> 00:04:43.127
Hardly any water means blank water.

78
00:04:43.427 --> 00:04:47.359
A, almost no. B, a lot of. C, plenty of.

79
00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:52.981
The answer is A: almost no.

80
00:04:54.117 --> 00:04:55.780
Which noun is uncountable?

81
00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.303
A, apple. B, rice. C, student.

82
00:05:02.867 --> 00:05:05.191
The answer is B: rice.

83
00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:08.953
According to the reading, where were hardly any people?

84
00:05:09.253 --> 00:05:12.872
A, at the park. B, at school. C, at home.

85
00:05:16.433 --> 00:05:18.909
The answer is A: at the park.

86
00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.880
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:23.717 --> 00:05:26.413
Describe your weekend using three quantifiers.

88
00:05:35.217 --> 00:05:36.624
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:36.924 --> 00:05:48.577
I had a lot of homework, so I stayed in for a few hours. There was plenty of food at home. In the evening hardly any people were on the street, so I walked for a little while.

90
00:05:48.877 --> 00:05:50.807
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:51.717 --> 00:05:57.306
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and quantifiers with countable and uncountable nouns.

92
00:05:57.606 --> 00:06:01.396
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:06:01.696 --> 00:06:05.173
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:05.473 --> 00:06:09.008
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

